WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.340 --> 00:00:03.330
- We are back and no, you do
not have to adjust your TV.

00:00:03.330 --> 00:00:06.510
Kelly did not become
an Asian man overnight.

00:00:06.510 --> 00:00:09.010
I'm Simu Liu filling
in for Kelly Clarkson.

00:00:09.010 --> 00:00:11.550
And you know, one of the things

00:00:11.550 --> 00:00:13.790
that I love about this
show is Kelly's passion

00:00:13.790 --> 00:00:16.270
for shining a light on
people, doing great things.

00:00:16.270 --> 00:00:18.060
And since it's my show for the day,

00:00:18.060 --> 00:00:20.050
I'm excited for you to meet my next guest.

00:00:20.050 --> 00:00:22.690
He's the fan founder of
the digital content creator

00:00:22.690 --> 00:00:23.890
Jubilee Media.

00:00:23.890 --> 00:00:25.550
Their mission is to bring people together

00:00:25.550 --> 00:00:27.400
through empathy and connection.

00:00:27.400 --> 00:00:30.330
Now you may have heard of one
of his most popular series

00:00:30.330 --> 00:00:33.640
called Spectrum, and he's
also one of my best friends.

00:00:33.640 --> 00:00:35.824
Please welcome Jason Y. Lee.

00:00:35.824 --> 00:00:39.109
(audience cheering)

00:00:39.109 --> 00:00:40.280
(Jason laughing)

00:00:40.280 --> 00:00:42.158
I know your story but for people who don't

00:00:42.158 --> 00:00:44.180
how did you found your company?

00:00:44.180 --> 00:00:45.350
How did you found Jubilee?

00:00:45.350 --> 00:00:46.183
- Yeah.

00:00:46.183 --> 00:00:48.272
As you know, I'm a child
of Korean immigrants.

00:00:48.272 --> 00:00:51.430
So I had a very traditional
view on what my life

00:00:51.430 --> 00:00:53.850
and what my career and what
success would look like.

00:00:53.850 --> 00:00:56.068
So after I graduated
from Penn, I went to Bein

00:00:56.068 --> 00:00:59.730
and in 2010 my 22nd birthday
happened to coincide

00:00:59.730 --> 00:01:00.820
with a Haiti earthquake.

00:01:00.820 --> 00:01:02.370
Which was kind of a crazy turn of events

00:01:02.370 --> 00:01:05.840
and I just felt like this
incredible need to do something.

00:01:05.840 --> 00:01:07.710
So I decided to go to
a New York subway stop

00:01:07.710 --> 00:01:10.480
to sing in a bus to raise
$100 dollars for Haiti

00:01:10.480 --> 00:01:12.470
which you know is a crazy
idea because unlike you

00:01:12.470 --> 00:01:15.060
and Kelly, I'm a terrible singer.

00:01:15.060 --> 00:01:15.893
But that day-

00:01:15.893 --> 00:01:16.850
- You're an A for effort singer.

00:01:16.850 --> 00:01:17.980
- Yes

00:01:17.980 --> 00:01:18.813
I try my best.

00:01:18.813 --> 00:01:21.700
That day we made 80 bucks,
I made my very first video,

00:01:21.700 --> 00:01:22.720
put it online.

00:01:22.720 --> 00:01:25.420
Within a week we had tens
of thousands of views

00:01:25.420 --> 00:01:26.450
and I think that's when,

00:01:26.450 --> 00:01:28.170
I kind of the light
bulb went off in my head

00:01:28.170 --> 00:01:29.530
of this is what I wanna do.

00:01:29.530 --> 00:01:30.990
I wanna create content.

00:01:30.990 --> 00:01:34.120
I wanna create a movement
where people believe in empathy

00:01:34.120 --> 00:01:36.800
and kindness and connection,
and that started Jubilee.

00:01:36.800 --> 00:01:39.240
So since then we have over 6 million,

00:01:39.240 --> 00:01:41.150
7 million subscribers now.

00:01:41.150 --> 00:01:43.550
We have had 2 billion views.

00:01:43.550 --> 00:01:45.550
We made our very first
feature documentary.

00:01:45.550 --> 00:01:47.690
So, I'm just so proud to
be starting a movement

00:01:47.690 --> 00:01:50.130
that provokes understanding
and human connection.

00:01:50.130 --> 00:01:51.050
- That's incredible.

00:01:51.050 --> 00:01:53.110
I, I've always loved your story

00:01:53.110 --> 00:01:55.390
and your propensity for, for empathy.

00:01:55.390 --> 00:01:58.350
I think that's why when they
asked me to host the show

00:01:58.350 --> 00:02:00.790
your name kind of
immediately came to mind.

00:02:00.790 --> 00:02:02.740
You're one of my favorite
people in the world.

00:02:02.740 --> 00:02:05.345
I'm so glad that America
now gets to meet you.

00:02:05.345 --> 00:02:07.360
So, so explain Spectrum.

00:02:07.360 --> 00:02:09.540
Explain what the Spectrum
series is all about.

00:02:09.540 --> 00:02:13.220
- So spectrum was one of
our very first viral shows

00:02:13.220 --> 00:02:16.410
and it really is a show
where we would bring people

00:02:16.410 --> 00:02:18.070
that seem like they're in the same group,

00:02:18.070 --> 00:02:20.530
like a very homogenous
group like do all men

00:02:20.530 --> 00:02:22.080
or do all teen moms think the same.

00:02:22.080 --> 00:02:23.670
And obviously the answer is no.

00:02:23.670 --> 00:02:24.650
But we put them in a warehouse

00:02:24.650 --> 00:02:26.670
and we'll have them line
up from strongly disagree

00:02:26.670 --> 00:02:28.139
all the way to strongly agree.

00:02:28.139 --> 00:02:29.590
And we'll ask questions

00:02:29.590 --> 00:02:32.128
that are intended to
provoke real conversation.

00:02:32.128 --> 00:02:34.430
I think one thing that we're
really missing right now

00:02:34.430 --> 00:02:36.160
is just true dialogue.

00:02:36.160 --> 00:02:38.050
It doesn't mean we have
to agree on everything

00:02:38.050 --> 00:02:40.085
but how can we actually
listen to each other,

00:02:40.085 --> 00:02:44.510
examine our beliefs and
see how we are similar

00:02:44.510 --> 00:02:45.790
and sometimes different?

00:02:45.790 --> 00:02:47.610
So we're really proud of it.

00:02:47.610 --> 00:02:50.180
We had over 300 million views to the show

00:02:50.180 --> 00:02:53.740
and what happened was a
lot of clubs and students

00:02:53.740 --> 00:02:56.043
and teachers actually
started using this format

00:02:56.043 --> 00:02:57.800
in their classrooms.

00:02:57.800 --> 00:02:58.820
And we said, you know what?

00:02:58.820 --> 00:02:59.690
We have to do something about it.

00:02:59.690 --> 00:03:02.150
So we actually decided to
make our very first game.

00:03:02.150 --> 00:03:04.080
So we actually made a card set

00:03:04.080 --> 00:03:05.330
based on Spectrum.
- [Simu Liu] Amazing.

00:03:05.330 --> 00:03:06.163
- Yeah.
- Amazing.

00:03:06.163 --> 00:03:08.210
And, and we're, we don't
have the cards with us,

00:03:08.210 --> 00:03:10.710
but, but you did bring
the game Spectrum here.

00:03:10.710 --> 00:03:11.543
- Yes.

00:03:11.543 --> 00:03:13.070
We have, you know, our
own way of playing it

00:03:13.070 --> 00:03:14.050
on the Kelly Clarkson show.

00:03:14.050 --> 00:03:15.200
- We're gonna play the abridged version.

00:03:15.200 --> 00:03:16.033
- That's right.

00:03:16.033 --> 00:03:18.050
And, and Ruben, the show's
fearless, warm up guy

00:03:18.050 --> 00:03:20.170
has actually agreed to play with us.

00:03:20.170 --> 00:03:21.003
So-

00:03:21.003 --> 00:03:22.070
- [Jason] Look at his outfit.
(Ruben laughs)

00:03:22.070 --> 00:03:22.903
- [Simu Liu] It's an amazing outfit.

00:03:22.903 --> 00:03:23.900
- I'm in.

00:03:23.900 --> 00:03:25.790
- So I'm gonna read a question, right?

00:03:25.790 --> 00:03:27.339
And, and each person will answer

00:03:27.339 --> 00:03:30.090
from strongly disagree to disagree,

00:03:30.090 --> 00:03:32.100
somewhat disagree, somewhat agree,

00:03:32.100 --> 00:03:34.130
agree and strongly agree.

00:03:34.130 --> 00:03:35.900
And, and then we're gonna talk about it.

00:03:35.900 --> 00:03:36.733
- That's right.

00:03:36.733 --> 00:03:38.610
And the key is this is
a safe space for all.

00:03:38.610 --> 00:03:40.510
So any, there's no right or wrong answer.

00:03:40.510 --> 00:03:42.380
And also there's no neutral

00:03:42.380 --> 00:03:44.100
but it's intended to
sometimes be meaningful.

00:03:44.100 --> 00:03:44.933
Sometimes it's fun.

00:03:44.933 --> 00:03:46.560
Sometimes it's spicy.

00:03:46.560 --> 00:03:49.320
So you, if you feel the need
to go there, let's go there.

00:03:49.320 --> 00:03:50.153
- [Ruben] Let's go.

00:03:50.153 --> 00:03:51.290
- Okay (laughs).
- [Ruben] Let's go.

00:03:51.290 --> 00:03:52.123
Let's go.

00:03:52.123 --> 00:03:52.987
- All right.

00:03:52.987 --> 00:03:53.820
- You ready?
- All right, America.

00:03:53.820 --> 00:03:54.653
You ready?

00:03:54.653 --> 00:03:55.486
Let's go.

00:03:55.486 --> 00:03:56.319
